   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion to recommit with instructions Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 189 - 233 (Roll no. 183).",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-22",
   "actionTime": "13:38:44",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H2311-2312)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "15:31:15",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on the motion to recommit with instructions, the Chair put the question on the motion and by voice vote, announced that the nays had prevailed. Ms. Rosen demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings on the motion to recommit with instructions until a time to be announced.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8A000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "15:31:05",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question on the motion to recommit with instructions was ordered without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "15:24:37",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the motion to recommit with instructions. The instructions contained in the motion seek to require the bill to reported back to the House with an amendment to add a subsection to the bill titled Protecting Affordable Healthcare for Older Americans.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36100",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "15:24:11",
   "committees": [
    {
     "name": "Judiciary Committee",
     "systemCode": "hsju00",
     "url": "https://api.congress.gov/v3/committee/house/hsju00?format=json"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Ms. Rosen moved to recommit with instructions to the Committee on the Judiciary. (text: CR H2274)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "15:23:42",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "14:42:07",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H.R. 372.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "14:41:37",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 372 with 1 hour of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit with or without instructions. Measure will be considered read. Bill is closed to amendments.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "14:41:32",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 209. (consideration: CR H2267; text of measure as reported in House: CR H2267)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-21",
   "actionTime": "13:43:31",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 209 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "2017-03-20",
   "actionTime": "19:28:49",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 209 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 372 with 1 hour of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit with or without instructions. Measure will be considered read. Bill is closed to amendments.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
